    57	
    58	f) Visual cleanliness
    59	- The scene is capped at two intended segments with modest distractor counts.
    60	- Rays and segment interiors are kept non-overlapping, including outside the input frame, which
    61	  avoids dense diagonal tangles in the expanded output.
    62	
    63	g) Color inference
    64	- No new color remapping is introduced. Blue remains the segment color and magenta remains the
    65	  trigger/ray color, so the only extra reasoning burden is the length code.
    66	
    67	i) New solver assumptions guaranteed by generation
    68	- At least one diagonal-aligned same-color blue pair exists, and no other color forms a longer
    69	  same-color diagonal pair.
    70	- Intended blue endpoints do not form accidental extra diagonal pairs across segments, so the
    71	  solver's "connect extremes on each key" logic recovers exactly the generated segments.
    72	- Cross-segment magenta triggers are not diagonally aligned, so the blue-vs-magenta color choice
    73	  remains unambiguous.
    74	- Full encoded rays may leave the input, but they never overlap reserved geometry, so painting
    75	  background-only cells is well-defined on the expanded canvas.
    76	"""
    77	
    78	from __future__ import annotations
    79	
    80	import random
    81	from itertools import combinations
    82	
    83	import numpy as np
    84	
    85	from arc_utils import get_bg
